Building medit
==============

medit is built with CMake.  A quick build with default options:

    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo
    cmake --build build -j"$(nproc)"
    sudo cmake --install build

By default this installs to /usr/local; pass
-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr to install into the system prefix.

Running the test suite:

    ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure

The suite needs a display; under a headless system run it as
`xvfb-run -a ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure`.


Dependencies
------------

Required:

    cmake >= 3.16, pkg-config, a C11 / C++14 compiler
    gtk+-3.0    >= 3.22
    glib-2.0    >= 2.56    (with gthread-2.0 and gmodule-2.0)
    libxml-2.0  >= 2.9
    intltool               (still required for translation merging)
    python3                (build-time only, for code generation)

Optional -- each is auto-detected and silently skipped when absent:

    vte-2.91    >= 0.52    integrated terminal
    gspell-1    >= 1.2     spell checking (plus hunspell and a dictionary)
    md4c, md4c-html >= 0.4 Markdown preview
    python3-dev, pygobject-3.0 >= 3.30
                           Python plugin support (-DMOO_WITH_PYTHON=yes)
    gdb                    the debugger plugin (a run-time dependency only;
                           the plugin builds without it)

On Debian and Ubuntu:

    sudo apt-get install build-essential cmake pkg-config intltool \
        libgtk-3-dev libxml2-dev libglib2.0-dev libvte-2.91-dev \
        libgspell-1-dev libhunspell-dev hunspell-en-us \
        libmd4c-dev libmd4c-html0-dev gdb

Note that GtkSourceView, Lua, xdgmime and EggSMClient are vendored in the
source tree; no system packages of those are needed or used.


Build options
-------------

    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=...      Debug, Release, RelWithDebInfo (default),
                                MinSizeRel
    -DMOO_WITH_PYTHON=yes|no    Python plugin support (default: auto)
    -DMOO_STRICT_MODE=ON        all warnings plus -Werror
    -DMOO_SANITIZE=address,undefined
                                build with the given sanitizers
    -DMOO_ENABLE_COVERAGE=ON    code-coverage instrumentation
    -DMOO_BUILD_MODULE=ON       also build the _moo Python module


Legacy autotools build
----------------------

An autotools build still exists but is unsupported and incomplete: it has no
detection for gspell, md4c, the wiki preview or gdb, so it cannot build
spell-checking, the page preview or the debugger.  Use CMake.
